00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
The Collector is a 2009 American horror film written by Patrick
Melton and Marcus Dunstan, and directed by Dunstan.

11
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
It stars Josh Stewart, alongside Michael Reilly Burke, Andrea Roth, Juan
Fernandez, Karley Scott Collins, Madeline Zima, and Robert Wisdom.

12
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
The film follows handyman Arkin O'Brien (Stewart) who, in order to pay a debt, decides to rob a house, only to find
out somebody with far more sinister intentions has already broken in and rigged it with multiple traps.

13
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
The original script, titled The Midnight Man, was at one point shopped as a spin-off prequel
to the Saw franchise, as an origin story for the villain John Kramer / Jigsaw.

14
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
The producers opposed the idea and dismissed it, but the strength of the script led to
writers Marcus Dunstan and Patrick Melton writing multiple Saw films.

15
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
The Collector was released on July 31, 2009, by Freestyle Releasing.

16
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
It received generally negative reviews from critics and
grossed $10.2 million against a $3 million budget.

17
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
A sequel, The Collection, was released theatrically on November 30, 2012.

18
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
The film explores themes of fight, burglar, psychopath, home, gore.

19
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
The tone is dark and intense.
